//HOW TO CREATE A REPO USING TERMINAL
Step 1 - git init
Step 2 - git add .
Step 3 - git status(to see changes)
Step 4 - git commit -m "message"
Step 5 - identify ur branch name
Step 6 - git push -u origin branchName

//HOW TO STAGE ALREADY EXISTING FILES
git commit -a -m "Updated project"

//GIT REMOTE COMMANDS
| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `git remote` | Lists remote names. |
| `git remote -v` | Shows remote names and their URLs. |
| `git remote add origin URL` | Adds a remote repository. |
| `git remote remove origin` | Removes a remote connection. |
| `git remote rename origin upstream` | Renames a remote. |
| `git remote get-url origin` | Displays the URL of a remote. |
| `git remote set-url origin URL` | Changes the URL of a remote. |
| `git remote show origin` | Shows detailed information about a remote. |

//HOW TO PULL CHANGES FROM GITHUB INTO YOUR VS CODE PROJECT
git pull origin main

//BRANCHES
Creating a branch - git branch branchName
Switching between branches - git switch (The name of the branch u want to switch to)
To check all branches - git branch -a

